  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the National Street Children&apos;s Movement: Pernambuco</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Movement of Street Children (MNMMR) Pernambuco Regional was set up in 1985, to defend the rights of young people and children, and to address the needs of street children, as well as to monitor the violence carried out against them. The aim of the organisation is to encourage children to participate in the construction of alternatives to improve their lives and guarantee their rights.

In Pernambuco, the work is divided into 4 main areas: the promotion and defence of rights; the promotion of children and adolescent&#x2019;s organisation and training; training for street educators; Strengthening internal organisation of the Movement.

MNMMR representatives sit on various state and municipal committees promoting the protection and rights of street children, and wider educational and health issues. Local Commissions of adults are responsible for making contact with the street children, and then encouraging them to form their own grass-roots organisations. These n&#xfa;cleos de base (grass-roots groups) are organised on the basis of solidarity, mutual aid, and co-responsibility.  CAFOD is supporting MNMMR with an institutional grant. IN 2007 we also provided funding for an institutional strengthening project with the accompanier of the Tarrafa project Hans Pepi.</narrative>
  </description>
